  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "Mara had tied white ribbons to the six orchard rows that morning. Each ribbon marked fruit promised to a different kitchen, including the kitchen where Ivo cooked for the school. Now the weather bell was ringing for an overnight frost. There were blankets in the shed, but the branches were too low to drape carelessly. “The bees ruined the early blossoms,” Mara said, repeating the explanation she had heard all week. “Perhaps covering these will keep them out.” Ivo looked at the darkening sky. They had a few hours, and no spare spring.",
      "evidence": [
        "e001"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "valley.frost",
        "mara.belief",
        "rows.total"
      ],
      "id": "night0.1",
      "drama": "night0"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the end of the first row, Mara bent over the damaged branch they had kept for comparison. The unopened buds were black inside; even flowers under a fine mesh bag had the same injury. A dated frost marker beside the branch matched the night of the damage. Bees had never entered that bag. “Cold,” she said at last. “We have been blaming the thing that brings us fruit.” The discovery did not mend a single blossom. It did change what she meant to shut out tonight.",
      "evidence": [
        "e002"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "trial.cause",
        "mara.observed_cause",
        "mara.belief"
      ],
      "id": "night1.1",
      "drama": "night1"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ivo brought out his father's field notebook, its swollen leather cover held shut with string. On the orchard bench, Mara opened a page showing cloth raised clear of the flowers and edges anchored against the ground. The words and drawing belonged together: a pocket of still air, not a wet blanket pressing on petals. She traced the drawing with a dirty finger, then said both instructions aloud. Ivo waited while she checked the page once more. This time she had attended to the whole method.",
      "evidence": [
        "e003"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "notebook.accessible",
        "mara.meme.air_gap",
        "mara.meme.anchor_edges"
      ],
      "id": "night2.1",
      "drama": "night2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mara made a shelter over the comparison branch: two short sticks, a roof of cloth, and stones closing the edges. She slid her hand underneath to check that no petal touched the fabric. A little cup of warm water remained warmer under that pocket than its twin on the bench. The small trial held its warmth. “That is something we can build,” she said. For the first time that evening, the blankets looked like a method instead of a heap of hopeful laundry.",
      "evidence": [
        "e004"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "trial.tested",
        "trial.protected",
        "trial.air_gap",
        "trial.anchored",
        "trial.retains_warmth",
        "trial.resistance",
        "valley.trial_cold"
      ],
      "id": "night3.1",
      "drama": "night3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ivo held out his long fork, the one with his initials burned into the handle. It could lift cloth above the branches without tearing it. “Borrow it until morning,” he said. Mara took it carefully; the tool was still his, even while her hands controlled it. Then he rolled up his sleeves. “You raise the roof; I'll carry stones and close the sides.” They would be able to move along the rows together, with neither leaving a half-finished shelter behind.",
      "evidence": [
        "e005"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "fork.owner",
        "fork.user",
        "ivo.willing"
      ],
      "id": "night4.1",
      "drama": "night4"
    },
    {
      "text": "Working together, they roofed all six rows. Mara lifted each sheet with the fork while Ivo planted supports and carried stones along the hem. They checked for hanging corners before moving on. At the last white ribbon, he held the cloth while she crawled underneath to free a snagged shoot. It was slow, awkward work, nothing like merely knowing a drawing. When they stood up, six low roofs lay along the orchard, with living flowers clear of their undersides.",
      "evidence": [
        "e006"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "rows.protected"
      ],
      "id": "night5.1",
      "drama": "night5"
    },
    {
      "text": "At sunrise Mara lifted the first shelter and found black centers beneath its undamaged roof. The overnight cold had grown more severe than the bench trial: even the correctly raised and anchored cloth could not resist it. She checked every covered row. All six marked rows had lost their blossoms, including the ones they had sheltered. The roofs still stood, and that made the loss harder to dismiss. Mara laid her palm on a support. Their work had been real; the cold had exceeded what their materials could bear.",
      "evidence": [
        "e007"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "rows.surviving",
        "valley.outcome",
        "valley.night_cold",
        "rows.resistance"
      ],
      "id": "night6.1",
      "drama": "night6"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mara wiped the fork's handle and returned it to Ivo. His initials emerged from beneath the soil. She gathered all six white ribbons and laid them beside the shut notebook. Beyond the bench, a bee landed on an unmarked weed in bloom. Mara left it undisturbed.",
      "evidence": [
        "e008"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "fork.user",
        "fork.returned",
        "fork.owner"
      ],
      "id": "night7.1",
      "drama": "night7"
    }
  ],
  "qa": [
    {
      "question": "What threatened the promised orchard fruit?",
      "answer": "An overnight frost threatened the blossoms on six marked rows. Mara wanted to preserve the fruit already promised to the community kitchens.",
